module Core

### The protocol for values that can produce an independent DEEP copy of themselves — a new object
### with its own lifetime, sharing no externally visible mutable state. `Copyable obeys Storable`
### (the capability rule: copy-able ⇒ store-able ⇒ assignable), so a `Copyable` value can also be
### `store`-d and assigned. `copy` is inserted wherever an independent duplicate is required — not
### only at assignment, but at every materialization point (e.g. building a value into a collection).
protocol Copyable obeys Storable
  ### Returns a deep, independent copy of this value.
  ### :returns: A copy of this value with its own valid lifetime and invariants.
  @readonly
  routine Me.copy() -> Me
